# RTX-30-ICN grading window: the table MISS / key-insert trap, isolated.
# (d2) COMPLIANT BY CONSTRUCTION, and it is NOT the table-building loop:
#   - the table never grows (an RVALUE miss mints the trap, rt_deref resolves it
#     via table_get_found, finds nothing, returns the default -- NO insert), so
#     the bucket chain length is constant across all 2,000,000 iterations;
#   - the key is a literal, so no per-iteration key allocation is added to the
#     window that does not belong to the ported path;
#   - the result is discarded, so the measured cost is the subscript's own
#     dispatch plus the two allocations the arm inherently performs.
# A table-BUILDING loop (`t[string(i)] := i`) is the MOTIVATING traffic but is
# NOT gradeable: it grows the chains, calls string() per iteration, and its cost
# per access rises monotonically. Measured separately, never used for the ratio.
procedure main()
  local i, t, x;
  t := table(0);
  t["seed"] := 1;
  every i := 1 to 2000000 do { x := t["absent"]; };
  write(x);
end
